==Strategy==
Note that this stage might be too much for players who have just unlocked it, so having all [[:Category:Empire of Cats Treasures|Treasures]] from [[Empire of Cats]], some [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cat]] [[True Form]]s and [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rares]] at level 25, at the very least, is strongly recommended before attempting this stage.

Since everything relevant in this stage has the [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] trait, bring as many good [[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|anti-Dark Cats]], especially [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] and [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ring Girl Cat]], as well as [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] with good anti-Dark abilities.

At the start, it is generally recommended to stall, as rushing could cause the wave with the Bun Buns to appear before Kurosawah, thus forcing the player into a fight with all the major threats at once.

Note that it is more efficient to farm XP in [[Growing Epic]] by selling the fruit afterwards, so this stage should lose priority once [[Legend Stages|Uncanny Legends]] is reached, at least during weekends.

